# Unity C# style (tier 1)

Tier 0: `docs/ENGINEERING_STANDARD.md` · Full Unity rules: `docs/UNITY_PLATFORM_STANDARD.md` §5–8

## Quick rules

- Prefer `[SerializeField] private` on MonoBehaviours; ScriptableObject configs use public read-only data fields (see full guide)
- ScriptableObject assets are never mutated at runtime; copy values locally when runtime state is needed
- Private fields: `camelCase` (no leading underscore); types/methods/properties: `PascalCase`
- Unity callbacks (`Awake`, `Update`, `FixedUpdate`, etc.) delegate to named methods; exception: trivial `timer += Time.deltaTime` only
- Member order: setup or lifecycle first, public API next, private helpers last; cleanup or teardown at the bottom
- Namespace matches assembly: `WebCasuals` (shared Framework), title namespace under `Assets/Game/` (e.g. `GhoulSmasher`)
- Framework must not reference Game
- Input System only; pointer + mouse + keyboard + touch
- No unbounded `Instantiate` in `Update`; pool or cap
- VContainer for DI; no Extenject in same project
- SRDebugger and heavy debug: development builds only
- WebGL: avoid hot-path allocations and unsupported native plugins
- Fail fast on missing refs; no silent null guards (see `fail-fast-no-null-guards.mdc`)
- Do not create enum-only files; nest enums in the owning type (e.g. `EnemyController.ZombieType`, config ScriptableObject, `LoadingProgressService.Stage`) — not a standalone `ZombieType.cs`
- UI text: TextMeshPro (`TMP_Text` / `TextMeshProUGUI`) only; use `StringBuilder` for runtime string composition

Read project `AGENTS.md` before structural changes.
